    "preamble": "Khouloud TAOUCHIKHT.pdf | Coordonnées\nwww.linkedin.com/in/khouloud-\ntaouchikht  (LinkedIn)\nlinktr.ee/khouloud_taouchikht\n(Personal)\ntaouchikht-khouloud.vercel.app/\n(Personal)\nPrincipales compétences\nArtificial Intelligence (AI)\nLarge Language Models (LLM)\nNatural Language Processing (NLP)",
    "certs": "AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner\nOracle Cloud Infrastructure Certified\nArchitect AssociateKhouloud TAOUCHIKHT\nÉtudiant en génie logiciel à l'INPT | Certifié AWS et Oracle\nRabat, Rabat-Salé-Kénitra, Morocco\nRésumé\nI’m a Software and AI Engineer with a passion for building smart,\nscalable, and reliable systems.\nI have a solid background in cloud computing, DevOps, and AI-\ndriven development, and I really enjoy solving complex problems that\nconnect these worlds. Whether it’s designing backend architectures,\ndeveloping full-stack features, or optimizing deployments, I focus on\ncreating systems that make a real difference.\nOutside of work, I love exploring emerging technologies,\nexperimenting with AI and data engineering projects, and learning\nnew ways to build intelligent applications. For me, technology is all\nabout continuous growth and finding creative ways to turn ideas into\nimpact.\nExpérience\nOracle\n2 ans 2 mois\nSoftware Engineer II\noctobre 2025 - Present  (5 mois)\nSoftware Engineer\njuillet 2024 - Present  (1 an 8 mois)\nAs a Software Engineer I at Oracle, I’ve been part of the team behind the\nLanguage Narrative, and Workbook Narrate features, initiatives aimed at\nmaking data analysis more intuitive, interactive, and AI-assisted for end users.\nI’ve worked on developing and optimizing data-driven insights and narrative\ngeneration features within Oracle Analytics Cloud, helping users easily\nunderstand and explain patterns behind their data visualizations.\n  Page 1 of 3\n   \nLanguage Narrative: Built and enhanced components that automatically\ngenerate descriptive summaries and contextual explanations for visualizations,\nhelping users interpret their data at a glance.\nWorkbook Narrate: Contributed to the narrative generation pipeline, integrating\nAI and statistical models to create clear, human-readable insights from\ncomplex workbook.\nThis experience deepened my expertise in AI-assisted analytics, data\nstorytelling, and cloud-based visualization systems, while reinforcing best\npractices in collaborative software engineering and scalable system design.\nSoftware Engineer Intern\njanvier 2024 - Present  (2 ans 2 mois)\nCasablanca-Settat, Morocco\nDuring my internship, I worked on Contextual Insights, a feature designed to\nmake data exploration more intuitive and insightful.\nThe goal was to allow users to interactively analyze data points within any\nchart and understand why certain values diffe, for example, why one region’s\nsales might be higher or lower than another"
